{{See also|List of United States senators from Georgia|2020 United States House of Representatives elections in Georgia}}

Due to the resignation of Republican senator [[Johnny Isakson]] at the end of 2019, both of Georgia's seats will be up for election this year. While the state overall still leans Republican, increased support for Democrats in [[Atlanta]]'s suburbs has made the state more competitive, with a close governor's race, multiple close U.S. House races, and many other close local office races resulting in Democratic gains in [[2018 Georgia gubernatorial election|2018]]. Both elections are seen as competitive.

