Four-term Republican [[Susan Collins]] was reelected by a wide margin in 2014. She is seeking a fifth term.<ref name="Kb2tz" />

Independent Green candidate, educator and activist Lisa Savage. <ref name="XSZQe" />

Democrats running included [[Speaker of the Maine House of Representatives|state House speaker]] [[Sara Gideon]],<ref name="u45ok" /> attorney Bre Kidman,<ref name="Kidman" /> and activist and [[2018 Maine gubernatorial election|2018 gubernatorial candidate]] Betsy Sweet.<ref name="Treacy" /> Gideon won the nomination.

Collins is polling neck-and-neck with or slightly behind Gideon. She has never faced a competitive election during her 24 years in the Senate even though Maine leans Democratic, as she has projected a centrist image. But she faces growing unpopularity due to her increasingly conservative voting record and her votes to confirm [[Brett Kavanaugh]] to the Supreme Court and to acquit Trump in his impeachment trial. Gideon raised over three times as much money as Collins in the first quarter of 2020.<ref name="Maine competitive" />
