J.J. Stitt, a farmer and gun shop owner, Neil Mavis, a former Libertarian Party candidate, and John Tompkins unsuccessfully challenged Inhofe for the Republican nomination.<ref name="lWdzQ" />

Democrats in the race included attorney [[Abby Broyles]], perennial candidate Sheila Bilyeu, 2018 [[Oklahoma's 5th congressional district|5th congressional district]] candidate Elysabeth Britt, and R.O. Joe Cassity Jr. Broyles won the nomination.

Libertarian candidate Robert Murphy and two Independents will also appear on the general election ballot.

Oklahoma is one of the most solidly Republican states and Inhofe is expected to be reelected with ease.{{Citation needed|date=September 2020}}
