Republican [[Shelley Moore Capito]] was easily elected after serving 14 years in the [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. House of Representatives]]. She was unsuccessfully challenged in the Republican primary by farmer Larry Butcher and Allen Whitt, president of the West Virginia Family Policy Council.<ref name="AWhitt" />

Environmental activist [[Paula Jean Swearengin]], a candidate for U.S. Senate in [[2018 United States Senate election in West Virginia|2018]],<ref name="bustle-knock-down" /> won the Democratic primary, beating former mayor of [[South Charleston, West Virginia|South Charleston]] Richie Robb and former [[West Virginia State Senate|state senator]] [[Richard Ojeda]], a nominee for the [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. House of Representatives]] in [[West Virginia's 3rd congressional district]] in [[2018 United States House of Representatives elections in West Virginia#District 3|2018]] and briefly a 2020 presidential candidate. Libertarian candidate David Moran will also appear on the general election ballot.
